# a2_gogc50
#
# donor      SHAFT-CPU off-path/p_alloc_probe (primary, n=3, gate byte-identical):
#                s3's lever set under MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1, MALLOC_TRIM_THRESHOLD_=0,
#                MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072, i.e. an allocator forced to hand pages back
#                peak 2,670,192 -> 2,611,260 kB = -2.2%,  wall 102 -> 138 s = +35%
#            BumbleBee x4_seal_pool_new (SEAL pool policy): peak +12.7%. LLAMA-Dealer allocator probes
#            (MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1: +0.004% peak, +32% wall): corroboration only (dealer line); its
#            MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 is a baseline setting (llama-dealer/MANIFEST.md:18).
# mechanism  allocator retention is a declared policy; lowering it changes no value. Go's heap target
#            is (GOGC/100 + 1) x live (2x at the default 100): a multiplier, unlike glibc arenas.
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: go:runtime_retained
# cost_class: free
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# basis      a1's decomposition:
#              go:runtime_retained                   153,806.1 MB   0.465 of the peak
#              rlwe.NewElement                       107,783.2 MB   0.326
#              ringqp.Ring.NewPoly                    42,121.8 MB   0.127
#              anon:residual                          15,420.4 MB   0.047
# rule 6     rlwe.NewElement by caller:
#              ckks.Evaluator.AddNew                                        45,088.8 MB
#              polynomial ... EvaluatePolynomialVectorFromPowerBasis
#                <- EvaluateBabyStep                                        34,232.9 MB
#              dft.(*Evaluator).SlotsToCoeffsNew                            14,492.9 MB
#              ckks.Evaluator.MulRelinNew                                   12,410.9 MB
#            all live at the census instant (working set); in-place variants would not remove them
#            (cf. MOAI-GPU s2).
# content    go:runtime_retained = present pages minus joined live objects
#            (JOIN|objects=308124|joined_bytes=161,197,363,376|anon_present=315,003,424,768); gctrace
#            before the peak 232422->232458->119470 MB:
#              heap headroom the collector holds  = 232.5 - 161.2  =  ~71 GB     <- what this step attacks
#              RSS that is not the Go heap at all = 315.0 - 232.5  =  ~82 GB     <- stacks, runtime, mappings
# lever      GOGC=50 (target 1.5x live instead of 2x).
# expected   ~60 GB off a 315 GB peak (~19%).
# cost       declared paid (collector runs ~2x as often; 235 cycles over 16,089 s).
# GOMEMLIMIT not used: a cap makes VmRSS track the cap (off-path.md: enabler only).
# no rebuild GOGC from the environment; same image as a1 (binary_md5 equal); RUN_META gogc=50.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# measured 2026-08-08, jobs 45926554 (clean), 45926555 (census):
#   peak      322,689,788 -> 253,243,940 kB   -66.2 GiB, -21.5%
#   wall           16,089 -> 15,434 s         4.1% FASTER
#   go:runtime_retained   153,806.1 -> 66,936.7 MB    -86.9 GB   <- predicted "roughly 71 GB"
#   ringqp.Ring.NewPoly    42,121.8 -> 42,127.9 MB    flat       <- as predicted, untouched
#   rlwe.NewElement       107,783.2 -> 120,680.4 MB   +12.9 GB
# remaining retained 66.9 GB vs ~82 GB predicted. Reclassified free (wall -4.1%). Donor verdicts
# (-2.2% for +35%; +12.7%) did not transfer: Go's retention is a multiplier on the live set.
# NewElement rise: census counts
#   a1   205,622 objects x 524,288 B  = 107,805.1 MB
#   a2   230,220 objects x 524,288 B  = 120,701.6 MB
# 24,598 more RNS polynomials (N = 2^16). Not settled: real or snapshot position (census trigger at
# 95% of the step's peak; step changes the RSS/liveness relation):
#   a1   trigger 307,560,716 kB   joined 161.2 GB live, 153.8 GB retained
#   a2   trigger 241,033,452 kB   joined 179.9 GB live,  66.9 GB retained
# instrument fix: trigger on a named phase marker.
#
# =============================================================================================
# re-measurement 2026-09-25 (one run per step, in-run census), position re-derived. a1's peak (3.42%
# below HWM), first Arion frame:
#   activation.ApproximatePolynomialChebyshevMT.func1          218.9 GB  71.1%   rank 1
#   matrix.CiphertextMatricesMultiplyWeightAndAddBiasMT.func1   45.1 GB  14.6%   rank 2
#   he.ParallelGenGaloisKeys.func1                              23.9 GB   7.8%   rank 3
#   (go:runtime_retained                                         5.3 GB           rank 5)
# object     dead share of rank 1 (heap dump lists uncollected objects under their site; gctrace
#            peak phase ~303 GB heap at GC start, ~160 GB live after, ~144 GB dead). Live part: paid
#            (threads). Dead part: GOGC (runtime_knob). Rank 2 is a3's object.
# prediction peak -15% to -25% vs a1, mostly rank 1; wall within spread. Refuted if rank 1 does not
#            shrink clearly more than other rows.
# measured   job 46917072:
#   peak 316,007,452 -> 248,137,676 kB  -21.5%   gate 3.9e-4 vs a0   census 3.1% below HWM
#   owners  a1 -> a2:  activation 218.9 -> 98.1 GB (-55%); WeightAndAddBias 45.1 -> 45.1; keys 23.9 -> 23.9;
#                      BootstrappingMT 14.5 -> 14.5.  GOGC acted on rank 1 only.
#   wall: program 18,547 s minus frozen 2,106 s = 16,441 s vs a1 14,521 s (+13%); retired clean
#   replicates (n=3, spread <2.5%): a2 5% faster; gctrace GC CPU share 0% in both.
#   cost_class stays declared free (n=1; in-run wall distorted by freeze counts).
